  "findings": [
    "Routed DQL answers in about 13 ms at 100K against about 413 ms direct (the baseline's warm MCP took 247 ms)",
    "Answering path listings with paths alone halved full listings routed: `ls --where type = task` (33,334 paths) 745 to 340 ms, `--format count` 304 to 142 ms; direct stays at 740 and 420 ms",
    "The remaining routed cost of full listings is evaluating every note's filter in the daemon and printing the paths"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Measured right after a release build; load was elevated, which slows both routes",
    "Equivalence compares one run's stdout per case, not every sample",
    "Host power, frequency, background load, and OS page cache are uncontrolled"
